@event seraphine_between_warning
# en: Not the North Stair
title [ee2ddf] = 别走北楼梯
# en: Seraphine stops {o} on the landing, puts a hand on {o.their} sleeve, and says, quite exactly, "Not the north stair tomorrow. The south one. Before the bell." Then she drifts off. {o} laughs, and then stops laughing, and asks you, "She's joking. Isn't she?"
text [505ee1] = 瑟拉芬在楼梯平台上拦住{o}，一只手搭在{o.their}袖子上，一字一句地说：“明天别走北楼梯。走南边那条。打铃之前。”说完就飘走了。{o}笑了，然后笑不出来了，转头问你：“她在开玩笑。对吧？”
# en: A dreamy student touching another's sleeve on a staircase landing, saying something quiet, while the other laughs.
scene [471cc2] = 楼梯平台上，一个神情恍惚的学生轻碰另一人的袖子，低声说了句什么，对方却笑了起来。
# en: "Take the south stair."
opt.left.label [ed1019] = “走南楼梯吧。”
# en: {o} takes the south stair, feeling silly. Nothing happens on the north stair, as far as anyone can tell. But that evening {o} sits beside Seraphine at supper, and she finishes {o.their} sentence for {o.them}, and {o} doesn't mind.
opt.left.say.1 [f20281] = {o}走了南楼梯，觉得自己有点傻。北楼梯上什么事也没发生，至少没人知道发生了什么。可那天晚饭时，{o}坐到了瑟拉芬旁边，她替{o.them}说完了一句话，而{o}并不介意。
# en: "Nobody knows what she means."
opt.right.label [10537c] = “谁也不知道她什么意思。”
# en: {o} takes the north stair out of principle, and meets a prefect with a notebook coming the other way, and a demerit for running. Seraphine looks faintly apologetic, a day early.
opt.right.say.1 [c2e81f] = {o}出于原则走了北楼梯，迎面撞上一个拿着小本子的级长，因为在楼梯上奔跑被记了一笔。瑟拉芬看上去有点抱歉——提前了一天。

@event seraphine_between_sentences
# en: The Other Half
title [11388f] = 另一半
# en: {~{o} has started a sentence three times today, and Seraphine has finished it three times, correctly, half a second early.|Seraphine answered a question {o} hadn't asked yet. {o} asked it anyway, to be sure. It was the right answer.|{o} told a joke at supper, and Seraphine laughed at the punchline before {o} got to it.} "It's not that I mind," {o} tells you. "It's that I can't tell if I'm still talking to her, or to next week."
text [5c551a] = {~{o}今天三次开口说话，瑟拉芬三次替{o.them}说完了，都提前半秒，而且都对。|瑟拉芬回答了一个{o}还没问的问题。{o}为了确认，还是问了一遍。答案是对的。|{o}晚饭时讲了个笑话，瑟拉芬在{o}讲到笑点之前就笑了。}“我不是介意，”{o}对你说，“我只是分不清自己是在跟她说话，还是在跟下个星期说话。”
# en: Two students side by side on a window seat, one talking, the other gazing out of the window and quietly saying the end of the sentence a moment before it comes.
scene [b2089e] = 窗台座上并排坐着两个学生，一个在说话，另一个望着窗外，在话说完之前就轻轻说出了结尾。
# en: Tell {o} it's how she listens
opt.left.label [defcd6] = 告诉{o}这是她倾听的方式
# en: {~"She only does it to people she likes," you say, which you aren't sure is true, and then find is. {o} starts leaving gaps in sentences, on purpose. Seraphine fills them, delighted.|"It means she's already enjoying the conversation," you say. {o} thinks about that for a whole afternoon and decides it's a compliment.|"Let her," you say. "She's usually right about the ending." {o} lets her. They get on, after that, in a way that skips the middle.}
opt.left.say.1 [4f7d51] = {~“她只对喜欢的人这样，”你说，其实你也不确定这是真的，后来发现确实如此。{o}开始故意在句子里留空。瑟拉芬高高兴兴地把空填上。|“这说明她已经在享受这场对话了，”你说。{o}想了整整一个下午，认定这是在夸人。|“随她去吧，”你说，“结尾她通常都说得对。”{o}随她去了。从那以后，她们相处得很好，好得直接跳过了中间。}
# en: Ask Seraphine to stay in today
opt.right.label [d12ef9] = 请瑟拉芬今天留在“今天”
# en: {~You tell Seraphine, gently, that {o} likes to say {o.their} own endings. "Oh," she says, "{o} will. On Thursday." She says nothing else all evening, and looks pleased about it.|Seraphine listens to you, nods, and then, very carefully, lets {o} finish every sentence for a week. It's somehow more unnerving.|"Today," Seraphine repeats, as if it were a foreign word. "I'll try." She manages most of a lunch.}
opt.right.say.1 [087f5d] = {~你温和地告诉瑟拉芬，{o}喜欢自己把话说完。“哦，”她说，“{o}会的。星期四。”那天晚上她什么都没再说，看上去还挺高兴。|瑟拉芬听你说完，点点头，然后小心翼翼地让{o}把每句话都说完，坚持了一个星期。不知怎么，这反而更让人发毛。|“今天，”瑟拉芬重复了一遍，像在念一个外语词。“我试试。”她坚持了大半顿午饭。}

@event tobias_between_sayings
# en: Where I'm From
title [42fa31] = 我老家那边
# en: Tobias said, at supper, that the soup "wanted more rain on it", which is what his mother says. {o} has been saying it all week, in a farmer's voice, with a pretend pitchfork. Tobias laughs from the belly every time. He's the only one who doesn't look like he's laughing.
text [2582de] = 托比亚斯晚饭时说，这汤“还欠一场雨”，这是他母亲的口头禅。{o}这一个星期都在学这句话，用农夫的腔调，还假装扛着一把干草叉。托比亚斯每次都笑得前仰后合。只有他看上去不像是在笑。
# en: A refectory table, a big broad-shouldered student laughing along a little too hard while a classmate across from him does an impression with a pretend pitchfork.
scene [79cf53] = 膳堂的桌边，一个宽肩膀的大个子学生笑得有点过头，对面的同学正假装拿着干草叉学人说话。
# en: Tell {o} to drop it
opt.left.label [5e932e] = 让{o}别再学了
# en: "That's his mum you're doing," you say. {o} goes red and stops. Tobias tells you, later, that he didn't mind, really, and apologises for you having to say anything, and then thanks you three times.
opt.left.say.1 [05bd1f] = “你学的是他妈妈，”你说。{o}脸一红，不学了。后来托比亚斯告诉你，他其实不介意，还为你不得不开口道了歉，然后谢了你三遍。
# en: Ask Tobias for the rest of the sayings
opt.right.label [47937c] = 请托比亚斯多讲几句家乡话
# en: You ask Tobias what else his mother says. He tells you, for an hour, with goats. By the end, {o} is laughing with him instead of at him, and asking what "a frost in the cream" means.
opt.right.say.1 [561e49] = 你问托比亚斯，他母亲还爱说些什么。他讲了一个小时，里面有好多山羊。到最后，{o}是在跟他一起笑，而不是笑他了，还问“奶油里结了霜”是什么意思。
# en: Tobias tries, and {o} does the voice again, and the table laughs again. Tobias laughs too. He eats the rest of his supper very fast and goes to the greenhouses.
opt.right.say.2 [9ffe56] = 托比亚斯刚开口，{o}又学起了那个腔调，满桌人又笑了。托比亚斯也笑了。他飞快地吃完剩下的晚饭，去了温室。

@event tobias_between_supper
# en: Proper Food
title [a04021] = 像样的饭菜
# en: {~{o} has been homesick all week and not saying so. Tobias noticed. He has borrowed a stove and is cooking, in the corner of the greenhouses, "proper food".|Tobias heard {o} say the refectory's bread tastes of nothing. There is now a loaf proving under a cloche in the greenhouse, and an invitation.|{o} missed a letter from home this month. Tobias is making a stew "big enough for a barn", and wants you to come and help eat it.} He asks if you'll come.
text [f99f28] = {~{o}想家想了一个星期，却一直没说。托比亚斯注意到了。他借了个炉子，正在温室的角落里做“像样的饭菜”。|托比亚斯听{o}说膳堂的面包吃起来什么味道都没有。现在温室的玻璃罩下正发着一团面，还附带一份邀请。|{o}这个月没收到家里的信。托比亚斯在炖一锅“够一个谷仓吃的”炖菜，想请你去帮忙吃。}他问你来不来。
# en: A greenhouse corner at night with a little stove, a big student stirring a pot, a homesick classmate wrapped in a blanket holding a bowl.
scene [4c2fbe] = 夜里温室的一角，一个小炉子，大个子学生在搅锅，一个想家的同学裹着毯子捧着碗。
# en: Bring something to the table
opt.left.label [ea2f5f] = 带点东西过去
# en: {~You bring cheese from the village. Tobias treats it like a holy relic. {o} eats three bowls and tells you about home, all of it, and it's a good evening.|You bring a jar of honey. Tobias's bread, it turns out, was waiting for exactly that. {o} laughs for the first time all week.|You bring the cider. Tobias tells the story of the goat that ate a hat. {o} tells one back. It's past midnight when you leave the greenhouse.}
opt.left.say.1 [fe199e] = {~你从山下小镇带了块奶酪。托比亚斯把它当圣物一样供着。{o}吃了三碗，把家里的事全讲给你听，那是个美好的夜晚。|你带了一罐蜂蜜。原来托比亚斯的面包等的就是它。{o}一个星期来第一次笑了。|你带了苹果酒。托比亚斯讲了那只吃掉帽子的山羊的故事。{o}也讲了一个。你离开温室时已经过了午夜。}
# en: Leave them to it
opt.right.label [4dcfa4] = 让他们俩自己吃
# en: {~You plead an essay. In the morning {o} looks better than you've seen {o.them} in weeks, and there's a heel of bread wrapped in a cloth on your desk.|You stay in. You can smell the stew from the dormitory. Tobias saves you a bowl, and apologises that it's cold.|You leave them to it. Somebody plays a fiddle badly in the greenhouses until late, and somebody else sings along.}
opt.right.say.1 [8950c1] = {~你推说要写论文。第二天早上，{o}的气色是你几个星期来见过最好的，你桌上还多了一块用布包着的面包头。|你待在宿舍。炖菜的香味一路飘到宿舍。托比亚斯给你留了一碗，还为它凉了道歉。|你让他们自己吃。温室里有人把小提琴拉得很糟，一直拉到很晚，还有人跟着唱。}

@event tobias_between_sulking
# en: The Ferns Are Sulking
title [703d3f] = 蕨类在生闷气
# en: {o} knocked over a tray of seedlings in the greenhouse last week, and swore at them. Now every plant on {o}'s bench leans away from {o.them}, and the ferns curl up when {o} comes in. Tobias, very gravely, says they're sulking. "They'll come round. But somebody's got to say sorry, and it'd better be {o}."
text [2b202b] = {o}上个星期在温室里打翻了一盘幼苗，还冲它们骂了句粗话。现在{o}工作台上的每一株植物都背着{o.them}长，{o}一进门，蕨类就卷起叶子。托比亚斯一本正经地说，它们在生闷气。“它们会消气的。可总得有人道个歉，最好是{o}。”
# en: A greenhouse bench of ferns all leaning pointedly away from one embarrassed student, a big student crouching to talk to them.
scene [b0271f] = 温室的工作台上，一排蕨类全都刻意背着一个尴尬的学生倾斜，一个大个子学生蹲下来跟它们说话。
# en: Help {o} say sorry to the ferns
opt.left.label [beda0b] = 帮{o}向蕨类道歉
# en: {o} kneels by the bench, mortified, while you hold the watering can and Tobias coaches in a whisper: "Lower. They like it lower." By the end of the lesson one fern has uncurled. Tobias claps {o} on the back hard enough to rattle the glass.
opt.left.say.1 [afbd9d] = {o}跪在工作台边，羞得无地自容；你拿着水壶，托比亚斯在一旁低声指导：“再低一点。它们喜欢低一点。”到下课时，有一株蕨舒展开了。托比亚斯拍了拍{o}的背，力气大得震响了玻璃。
# en: Tell {o} it's only plants
opt.right.label [6f8ffa] = 告诉{o}那只是植物
# en: {o} laughs, relieved, and goes back to the bench. The ferns go on leaning away from {o} for the rest of term, and {o} quietly moves benches in the spring. Tobias doesn't say anything, which, for Tobias, is saying a great deal.
opt.right.say.1 [d4a8f0] = {o}松了口气，笑着回到工作台。整个学期，那些蕨类都背着{o}长，到了春天，{o}悄悄换了张工作台。托比亚斯什么都没说——对托比亚斯来说，这已经说明了很多。

@event maud_between_soup
# en: Carry This, Dearie
title [1569ee] = 把这个端去，孩子
# en: Old Maud catches you on the path with a covered pot. "{o}'s abed with a chill, dearie, and too proud to say so. Take this up. Hot, mind. And sit with {o.them} till it's eaten. That's the important bit, the sitting. Soup's just the excuse."
text [1e24f2] = 老莫德端着一口盖着的锅在小路上拦住你。“{o}着了凉躺下了，孩子，又好面子不肯说。把这个端上去。趁热，当心。再坐在{o.them}旁边看着吃完。要紧的是坐着陪的那一会儿。汤只是个由头。”
# en: An old woman in a garden apron handing a covered pot to a student at her cottage door, the lamp lit behind her.
scene [b0cf6e] = 小屋门口，一个系着园艺围裙的老妇人把一口盖着的锅递给一个学生，身后亮着灯。
# en: Carry it, and sit with {o}
opt.left.label [0ac78f] = 端上去，陪{o}坐坐
# en: You carry the pot up three flights without spilling, and sit on the end of {o}'s bed while {o} eats it. {o} talks, eventually, about being ill and far from home. The soup does what Maud's soup does. So, you think, does the sitting.
opt.left.say.1 [9226b4] = 你端着锅爬了三层楼，一滴都没洒，然后坐在{o}床尾看{o}吃。{o}终于开口了，说起生病、说起离家很远。汤起了莫德的汤该起的作用。你想，陪着坐的那一会儿也是。
# en: Leave it at {o}'s door
opt.right.label [122a93] = 放在{o}门口
# en: You knock, leave the pot on the step, and hurry off to your essay. The pot comes back to Maud empty. Maud looks at you over her spectacles. "Soup's only half of it, dearie," she says, and you understand what she meant a fortnight later.
opt.right.say.1 [9b2d39] = 你敲了门，把锅放在台阶上，就匆匆赶回去写论文。锅空着回到了莫德那儿。莫德从眼镜上方看着你。“汤只是一半，孩子，”她说。两个星期后你才明白她的意思。

@event maud_between_beans
# en: The Bean Rows
title [d28c57] = 豆架
# en: Someone cut through Maud's garden in the dark and took out a whole row of runner beans. You know it was {o}, chasing a runaway hat. {o} knows you know. Maud is standing at the end of the row with her hands on her hips, saying, to nobody in particular, "Only, I'd like to know, that's all."
text [9ea25d] = 有人摸黑抄近路穿过莫德的菜园，踩倒了一整排红花菜豆。你知道是{o}，为了追一顶被风吹跑的帽子。{o}也知道你知道。莫德双手叉腰站在那排豆架尽头，不冲着谁地说：“我就是想知道，没别的。”
# en: A trampled row of runner beans beside a cottage garden, a goat looking innocent, an old woman with her hands on her hips.
scene [39f42c] = 小屋菜园边，一排红花菜豆被踩得东倒西歪，一只山羊一脸无辜，一个老妇人双手叉腰。
# en: Get {o} to own up
opt.left.label [07b848] = 劝{o}去认错
# en: {o} goes and owns up, scarlet. Maud listens, nods, and hands {o} a trowel. By evening the beans are re-staked and {o} has been given soup, a lecture on beans, and a standing invitation to Sunday weeding.
opt.left.say.1 [0eef9b] = {o}满脸通红地去认了错。莫德听完，点点头，递给{o}一把小铲子。到傍晚，豆架重新立好了，{o}得到了一碗汤、一堂关于豆子的课，还有一份星期天来除草的长期邀请。
# en: {o} won't. "She'll tell the headmistress." She wouldn't, you know she wouldn't, but {o} won't hear it. Maud re-stakes the beans herself, slowly, and you feel every pole.
opt.left.say.2 [2ea4ce] = {o}不肯去。“她会告诉院长的。”她不会的，你知道她不会，可{o}听不进去。莫德自己慢慢重新立好了豆架，每一根杆子你都看在眼里。
# en: Re-stake them yourself
opt.right.label [b23090] = 自己去把豆架立好
# en: You come back at dawn and re-stake the row before Maud's up. She finds you at it. "Funny," she says, "how a person's bean rows mend themselves." She doesn't ask. She gives you a jar of honey, and another one "for your friend".
opt.right.say.1 [e3fafb] = 你天一亮就回去，赶在莫德起床前把那排豆架立好了。她撞见你正在干活。“真怪，”她说，“这豆架怎么自己就好了。”她没有问。她给了你一罐蜂蜜，又给了一罐，“给你朋友的”。

@event maud_between_advice
# en: Two Weeks Later
title [df9b72] = 两个星期后
# en: {o} went to Old Maud about a friend who'd stopped speaking to {o.them}, and came back with this: "Water the roots, dearie, not the leaves." {o} has been turning it over for days. "Is it about plants? It's not about plants. Is it?"
text [5f295d] = 有个朋友不跟{o.them}说话了，{o}去找老莫德，带回来这么一句：“浇根，孩子，别浇叶子。”{o}琢磨了好几天。“是说植物吗？不是说植物吧。是吗？”
# en: Two students on a garden bench puzzling over something, an old woman with a watering can walking away from them, smiling to herself.
scene [e68e99] = 花园长凳上两个学生对着什么苦思冥想，一个拎着水壶的老妇人从他们身边走开，自顾自地笑着。
# en: Puzzle it out together
opt.left.label [3d38bc] = 一起琢磨
# en: You sit up half the night on it. Somewhere around midnight you both get it at once: stop arguing about the thing, and go and see the person. {o} does, the next day. It works. Maud, told, says "did I say that, dearie?", which you choose to take as modesty.
opt.left.say.1 [17977e] = 你们熬了大半夜。快到午夜时，你们俩同时想通了：别再为那件事争了，去见那个人。第二天{o}去了。成了。告诉莫德时，她说：“我说过这话吗，孩子？”你们决定把这当作谦虚。
# en: "Give it two weeks."
opt.right.label [6c4246] = “过两个星期就懂了。”
# en: "Maud's advice takes two weeks," you say. {o} rolls {o.their} eyes. A fortnight later {o} stops you in a corridor, shining: "The roots! It was the roots!" You still don't know what {o} worked out. You decide not to ask.
opt.right.say.1 [3faa77] = “莫德的建议要过两个星期才见效，”你说。{o}翻了个白眼。两个星期后，{o}在走廊里拦住你，两眼放光：“根！说的是根！”你至今不知道{o}想明白了什么。你决定不问了。

@event thorne_between_hard
# en: Hm.
title [52fec0] = 嗯。
# en: Thorne has handed {o}'s essay back for the third week running, more red ink than black. "Hm," he said, which is all he said. {o} is close to tears in the corridor. "He hates me. He doesn't do this to anyone else. Will you talk to him? He listens to you."
text [027122] = 索恩教授已经连续三个星期把{o}的论文退回来，红墨水比黑墨水还多。“嗯，”他说，就只说了这一个字。{o}在走廊里快哭了。“他讨厌我。他从不这样对别人。你能去跟他说说吗？他听你的。”
# en: A severe old professor handing back an essay covered in red ink, a student staring at it, a third student at the next desk.
scene [3101c1] = 一位严厉的老教授递回一篇布满红墨水的论文，学生盯着它，邻桌坐着第三个学生。
# en: Talk to Thorne
opt.left.label [a7a48c] = 去找索恩教授谈
# en: Thorne hears you out, unmoved, and then says, "The student in question is the only one in that class worth correcting." He doesn't change a word of the red ink. But the next essay comes back with one line at the bottom, in black: "Better." {o} frames it.
opt.left.say.1 [f64255] = 索恩教授面无表情地听你说完，然后说：“你说的那位学生，是那个班上唯一值得纠正的人。”他一个红字都没改。可下一篇论文发回来时，末尾用黑墨水写了一行：“有进步。”{o}把它裱了起来。
# en: "Flattery on another's behalf is still flattery," says Thorne, and turns back to his marking. You leave, having made it, possibly, slightly worse.
opt.left.say.2 [c798e1] = “替别人说好话，也还是说好话，”索恩教授说着，转回去批改作业。你离开了，大概把事情弄得更糟了一点。
# en: Read the red ink with {o}
opt.right.label [854dee] = 和{o}一起读那些红字
# en: You go through it line by line with {o}. Half of it, you point out, is Thorne arguing with {o}'s ideas, which he only does with ideas he thinks are worth it. {o} looks at the essay differently after that. So, for a moment, do you.
opt.right.say.1 [d4be4d] = 你和{o}逐行看下去。你指出，其中一半是索恩教授在跟{o}的观点争论，而他只跟他认为值得的观点争论。从那以后，{o}看那篇论文的眼光不一样了。有那么一会儿，你也是。

@event thorne_between_flattery
# en: Allergic
title [0c41c4] = 过敏
# en: {o} has a plan for the next practical mark: to be nice to Professor Thorne. Very nice. There's a speech about his "legendary career", and a rose. {o} is heading for his office now. You know, as everyone who has met Thorne knows, that he is allergic to flattery, possibly literally.
text [5fc9e0] = {o}为下一次实践课的分数想了个办法：对索恩教授好一点。非常好。准备了一段关于他“传奇生涯”的发言，还有一朵玫瑰。{o}正往他的办公室走去。你知道，所有见过索恩教授的人都知道，他对奉承过敏，也许字面意义上也是。
# en: A student bowing slightly too low to a severe old professor in a corridor, holding out a single rose, while a friend behind them winces.
scene [c3525d] = 走廊里，一个学生向一位严厉的老教授鞠躬鞠得太低，手里举着一朵玫瑰，身后的朋友不忍直视。
# en: Head {o} off
opt.left.label [dec8c3] = 把{o}拦下来
# en: You catch {o} on the stair and explain, quickly, about Thorne. {o} goes pale and gives you the rose. You keep it on your desk. It's a perfectly nice rose; it's just in no danger of reaching Thorne.
opt.left.say.1 [32f468] = 你在楼梯上截住{o}，飞快地讲了讲索恩教授的事。{o}脸色发白，把玫瑰给了你。你把它放在书桌上。那是朵很好的玫瑰；只是再也没有落到索恩教授手里的危险了。
# en: Let {o} find out
opt.right.label [548892] = 让{o}自己去发现
# en: You hear about it at supper, from four people. Thorne listened to the speech in silence, took the rose, and set {o} an additional essay on "the uses of sincerity". {o} doesn't speak to you for a day, and then laughs about it for a month.
opt.right.say.1 [7b7cdd] = 晚饭时，你从四个人那里听说了这件事。索恩教授一言不发地听完发言，收下玫瑰，然后给{o}加布置了一篇论文，题目是《论真诚的用处》。{o}一天没理你，然后笑了一个月。

@event isolde_between_remembers
# en: The Second Week
title [658fcc] = 第二个星期
# en: The Headmistress stops beside {o} in the Great Hall, pleasant and unhurried. "{o}. How is the potion that turned the stairs blue? The second week, I believe. Nobody's ever managed that shade since." She moves on. {o} wants the floor to swallow {o.them}. "She remembers. She remembers everything."
text [f61cc1] = 院长在大礼堂里停在{o}身边，和气而从容。“{o}。那瓶把楼梯染成蓝色的药剂怎么样了？我记得是第二个星期。之后再没人调出过那种蓝。”她走开了。{o}恨不得地板把{o.them}吞下去。“她记得。她什么都记得。”
# en: A tall pale headmistress pausing in the Great Hall beside a student, smiling pleasantly, while the student turns slowly crimson.
scene [416f54] = 大礼堂里，一位高挑苍白的院长在一个学生身边停下，和气地微笑，那学生的脸慢慢涨得通红。
# en: "She remembered your name."
opt.left.label [d7696b] = “她记得你的名字。”
# en: "She remembered your name, and the shade of blue," you say. "That's a compliment, from her." {o} doesn't believe you. But {o} walks a little taller past the Headmistress's tower for the rest of the term.
opt.left.say.1 [d2e943] = “她记得你的名字，还记得那种蓝，”你说，“从她嘴里说出来，这是夸奖。”{o}不信。可这个学期剩下的日子里，{o}经过院长塔时腰板都挺得直了些。
# en: Confess your own first week
opt.right.label [94693b] = 坦白你自己的第一周
# en: You confess your own first-week disaster, and that you live in fear of the day she mentions it. {o} laughs until {o} has to sit down. You feel it was worth it, nearly.
opt.right.say.1 [1771ce] = 你坦白了自己第一周闯的祸，还有你一直害怕她哪天提起这件事。{o}笑个不停，笑到{o}只好坐下来。你觉得，这差不多值了。

@event isolde_between_complaint
# en: An Appointment
title [783267] = 一次约见
# en: {o} has written a complaint about a lecturer who marks unfairly, and has an appointment with the Headmistress to deliver it in person. {o} has rewritten it eleven times. "Come with me," {o} says. "Just stand there. I can't do it alone."
text [a00cd5] = {o}写了一封投诉信，投诉一位打分不公的讲师，还约好了要亲手交给院长。{o}已经改写了十一遍。“陪我去吧，”{o}说，“就站在那儿。我一个人做不到。”
# en: The door of a tall tower office ajar, a student hesitating on the threshold with a folded letter, a friend at their shoulder.
scene [13454e] = 高塔办公室的门半开着，一个学生攥着一封折好的信在门口犹豫，朋友站在身旁。
# en: Go in with {o}
opt.left.label [a2fd4f] = 陪{o}进去
# en: The Headmistress reads the letter slowly, asks {o} two questions, each placed like a chess piece, and then says, "Thank you. That was not easy." The marks are reviewed by the end of the month. {o} doesn't stop shaking until supper.
opt.left.say.1 [275264] = 院长慢慢读完信，问了{o}两个问题，每个都像落下的一枚棋子，然后说：“谢谢你。这并不容易。”到月底，那些分数被重新审核了。{o}一直抖到晚饭时才停下。
# en: The Headmistress listens pleasantly and says she will "look into it". {o} can't tell, afterwards, whether that means yes or no. Neither can you. Nothing seems to change for a month, and then, quietly, something does.
opt.left.say.2 [0399ee] = 院长和气地听着，说她会“调查一下”。事后，{o}分不清那是答应还是拒绝。你也分不清。一个月里似乎什么都没变，然后，悄无声息地，有些事变了。
# en: Help {o} rewrite it once more
opt.right.label [1cfb8e] = 帮{o}再改一遍
# en: You sit with {o} and cut the letter down to six lines, all of them true. {o} goes in alone, in the end, and comes out ten minutes later, astonished. "She read every line. Then she asked about the third one."
opt.right.say.1 [b418fa] = 你和{o}坐下来，把信删到六行，每一行都是实话。最后{o}是一个人进去的，十分钟后出来，一脸惊讶。“她每一行都读了。然后问起了第三行。”
